# WALL WRESTLING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Wall Wrestling is a partner-based combat drill performed against a wall or cage to develop positional dominance, pressure application, takedown control and combat-specific conditioning.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer exercises for clinch-based combat sports and self-defense.

---

# Philosophy

Many fights are decided against a wall.

Not in open space.

Wall Wrestling develops the ability to control an opponent while maintaining posture, balance and continuous pressure under realistic constraints.

CAS selects this exercise whenever positional dominance and cage or wall efficiency are priorities.

